# The Moore machine state of an FFI program and its computation graph (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Terms"). A program is a closed term, a state
# λk. k output transition, with k in neither field: output is what the state asks the FFI to do, and transition takes
# the input symbol, a closed term, to the next state. The FFI's meaning is the step-by-step reading of x ∥
# moore_state_type for any x, not of x itself, which unfiltered would bring stray terms; moore_state_type is the
# criterion of one step (java_ffi/moore_types).
#
# An output ends its branch with an answer, or runs an expression. An expression is one of three nodes, with no control
# flow:
# - call: a method, λk. k ["owner", "name", "descriptor"], and a Scott list (prelude/list) of expressions, an instance
#   method's receiver being the first;
# - new: a class, λk. k "owner", a constructor's descriptor, λk. k "descriptor", and a Scott list of expressions: the
#   JVM's new instruction with the constructor, a method;
# - decode: a primitive value in the format natives read, a Scott boolean
#   (native_types/boolean) or a bit tuple (java_ffi/bits), which stands at a primitive parameter and is read as the type
#   the descriptor gives there.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "java_ffi") "moore_types")
λ _ _ _ _ moore_state_type _ _ _
# state:
# The state of an output and a transition.
. (λtuple. tuple λoutput transition k. k output transition)
λ state
# finish:
# The output that ends a branch with the answer.
. (λtuple. tuple λanswer on_finish on_run. on_finish answer)
λ finish
# run:
# The output that runs the expression.
. (λtuple. tuple λexpression on_finish on_run. on_run expression)
λ run
# call:
# The node of a method call.
. (λtuple. tuple λmethod arguments on_call on_new on_decode. on_call method arguments)
λ call
# new:
# The node of the new instruction with a constructor.
. (λtuple. tuple λclass descriptor arguments on_call on_new on_decode. on_new class descriptor arguments)
λ new
# decode:
# The node of a primitive value.
. (λtuple. tuple λvalue on_call on_new on_decode. on_decode value)
λ decode
. export state finish run call new decode moore_state_type
